From 0000000000000000000000000000000000000000 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Dan Yocom <630234+danyocom@users.noreply.github.com>
Date: Thu, 17 Sep 2026 21:11:37 -0400
Subject: [PATCH 10/14] Organise the in-game reset by dispatcher rather than by
 layer

The dispatcher table and its function pointers cost more to read than they
saved to write. They existed so that adding a dispatcher touched one table row,
which only pays off with many more versions than there are; at three, the
indirection is the harder half to follow.

Replacing them with an explicit chain of searches and two switches removes the
table, the descriptor struct, and six thunks that existed only to fill it in,
and lets each search inline its own validation instead of splitting it across a
function with a fixed signature.

What made the table worth having in the first place is kept: the search itself
is still written once, since iterating every candidate, rejecting a second
match and bounds checking are the parts worth getting right in one place.

The files are now grouped by dispatcher instead of by layer, so a dispatcher's
pattern, checks and patch code sit together rather than in three files, and the
whole feature moves into a directory of its own. The generated patch code is
unchanged, and all five sections are the same size as before.
